Access Modifiers in Java (Roman Urdu me)

Java me access modifiers wo keywords hain jo decide karte hain class, variable, method ka access scope (kaun use kar sakta hai).

1. public

Access: Har jagah se accessible (same class, same package, different package, subclass).

Example:

public int age;


Matlab koi bhi class is age ko access kar sakti hai.

2. private

Access: Sirf usi class ke andar accessible jahan define hua hai.

Example:

private String name;


Dusri class se direct access nahi hoga, getter/setter use karna padega.

3. protected

Access:

Same package ke andar → accessible

Different package → sirf subclasses me accessible

Example:

protected void display() { }

4. default (package-private)

Access: Agar koi modifier nahi lagaya toh default hota hai → sirf same package me accessible.

Example:

int count; // default


| Modifier  | Same Class | Same Package | Subclass (diff package) | Other Packages |
| --------- | ---------- | ------------ | ----------------------- | -------------- |
| public    | ✅          | ✅            | ✅                       | ✅              |
| protected | ✅          | ✅            | ✅                       | ❌              |
| default   | ✅          | ✅            | ❌                       | ❌              |
| private   | ✅          | ❌            | ❌                       | ❌              |
